# SDD Summary — environment variables
#
# You normally need NONE of these.
#
# The deploy script wires up whatever your editor needs, and credentials come
# from login(), which parses your Genesys Authorization URL and stores the
# result under .sdd-summary/. Copy this file to .env only if you need an
# override for a non-standard setup.
#
# IMPORTANT: never commit .env.

# ─── Host selection ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set by the deploy script to "cursor" or "kiro". It selects the host-specific
# guidance the server emits — chiefly HOW the agent should spawn the parallel
# scoring subagents for an eval run, since the two editors expose different
# mechanisms under different names. Unset yields deliberately host-neutral
# wording, which is correct but less specific.
# SDDSUM_HOST=kiro

# ─── Storage paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On Cursor these are set to workspace-relative paths using ${workspaceFolder},
# which keeps your data in the project you have open.
#
# On Kiro they are deliberately LEFT UNSET. Kiro does not expand
# ${workspaceFolder} — the placeholder would reach the server verbatim — but it
# does launch the server with the workspace root as its working directory, so
# the server's own defaults already resolve to the project root. Set these by
# hand only when running the server outside a normal deploy.

# Where OAuth config and tokens are written. Defaults to .sdd-summary/ at the
# project root, located by walking up for a .kiro/, .cursor/ or .git/ marker.
# SDDSUM_STORAGE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/.sdd-summary

# Where lifecycle data (transcripts, test cases, eval runs) is written.
# Defaults to .summaryconfig-lifecycle/ at that same project root.
# SDDSUM_LIFECYCLE_PATH=/absolute/path/to/project/root

# ─── Genesys credentials — AVOID SETTING THESE ───────────────────────────────
# GENESYS_CLIENT_ID shadows the stored config. If it is set, login() will
# authenticate against whichever org this ID belongs to, ignoring the
# Authorization URL you passed — which silently logs you into the wrong org.
# Let login() manage the client ID and region instead.
#
# GENESYS_CLIENT_ID=
# GENESYS_REGION=

# GENESYS_CLIENT_SECRET is NOT required. The user login flow
# (Authorization Code + PKCE) does not use a client secret. It exists only for
# the vestigial machine-to-machine client credentials fallback.
# GENESYS_CLIENT_SECRET=
